* lvs_include_hart -- LVS macro/std-cell CDL set for the MCU_hart block.
*
* BLOCK level, so there is deliberately NO pad content: no tphn pad .spi, no
* pad_filler_stubs.  Compare with lvs_include_chip_penta, which needs both.
*
* THE RULE THIS FILE EXISTS TO ENFORCE: every cell the design instantiates must
* have a subckt here.  When one is missing Pegasus does not warn, it ABORTS:
*   ERROR (NVN-13010): Cell <name> is not defined.
* That is what killed the 2026-08-16 TCM swap (sram1p8k_hvt_pg absent from
* lvs_include_chip) and it is flagged again at lvs_include_chip_penta:11.
* prep_top_netlist_hart.sh prints a macro census of the actual netlist for
* exactly this cross-check -- read it against the list below before every run.
*
* rom2k_hvt_pg is the NEW 2048x32 boot ROM (A[10:0], SIZE 156.525 BY 181.41).
* It has never appeared in any other include file in this tree.  rom_hvt_pg,
* the 16 KiB plate, stays listed: a config staged before the 8 KiB flip binds
* rom0 to it, and an unused .include_cdl costs nothing.
*
* sram1p8k_hvt_pg is the PRIVATE TCM inside hart_tile.  The tile is an excluded
* hcell in this flow, but the tile netlist is CONCATENATED into the source
* netlist (pvs/hart_tile.lvs.v; a boxed or stubbed tile aborts the compare at
* the matcher threshold), so the macro is present in the CDL and must resolve.
* sram1p16k_hvt_pg is the shared bulk-RAM / NPU-staging family at MCU level.
